{
  "id": "query/basics/12_instantiations",
  "topic": "query",
  "subtopic": "basics",
  "title": "Answers through instantiations",
  "summary": "References and the call graph include what instantiations and macro expansions resolve, each marked with its `via`",
  "prose": "A use the written code leaves open — a dependent call in a template, a name\nin a macro body — answers with `\"via\": \"instantiation\"` or\n`\"via\": \"expansion\"`; the written code's answers carry no `via`. A caller\ncarries one only when instantiations make all its calls.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "box.h",
      "text": "#pragma once\n\nstruct Box {\n    void open();\n};\n\nvoid reset();\n\n#define RESET_ALL reset()\n",
      "markers": []
    },
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "#include \"box.h\"\n\nvoid Box::open() {}\n\nvoid reset() {}\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nvoid twice(T& item, Box& box) {\n    item.open();\n    box.open();\n}\n\nvoid run(Box& box) {\n    twice(box, box);\n}\n",
      "markers": []
    },
    {
      "path": "measure.h",
      "text": "#pragma once\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nvoid measure(T& item) {\n    item.open();\n}\n",
      "markers": []
    },
    {
      "path": "use.cpp",
      "text": "#include \"box.h\"\n#include \"measure.h\"\n\nvoid use(Box& box) {\n    measure(box);\n    RESET_ALL;\n}\n",
      "markers": []
    }
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "name": "test",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "label": "$ clice index",
          "value": {
            "stdout": "Indexed 2 translation units in #s: 4 file shards (# KB), 8 symbols.\nSession log: ${WS}/.clice/logs/${SESSION}",
            "exit": 0
